# Security Rules (Non-negotiable)

- Never expose `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (or any service role key) to the frontend
- Never call `getSession()` server-side (can be spoofed) — use `getUser()`
- Always validate the user server-side before returning data from `app/api/**`
- Do not put secrets in `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` — only anon URL/key for Supabase Auth client
- Server API keys (`ANTHROPIC_*`, `TAVILY_*`, `WEATHER_*`, `HF_TOKEN`) stay server-only
- Prefer cookie-based SSR sessions via `@supabase/ssr`; never store auth tokens in `localStorage`
- Enforce RLS with `auth.uid()`; do not rely on client-supplied user IDs
